      <div class="step-task"><span class="task-label">DO THIS · EDIT OR ADD A PROJECT</span>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Find the list.</strong> With <code>profile.js</code> open, search for <code>projects:</code> and click the first match so your cursor is on that line.</li>
          <li><strong>Prefer editing a sample first.</strong> Scroll to the first object that starts with <code>title: 'Campus Resource Finder'</code> (or another sample). Change <code>title</code>, <code>slug</code>, <code>summary</code>, <code>skills</code>, and <code>link</code> to your project. Keep the commas and quotes.</li>
          <li><strong>What each field is for</strong>
            <ul>
              <li><code>title</code> — name shown on the card</li>
              <li><code>slug</code> — URL piece only (lowercase, hyphens, no spaces), e.g. <code>inventory-tracker</code> → <code>/projects/inventory-tracker/</code></li>
              <li><code>summary</code> — one or two sentences on the home page</li>
              <li><code>overview</code> / <code>problem</code> / <code>approach</code> / <code>outcome</code> — longer story on the project detail page</li>
              <li><code>skills</code> — short tags (array of strings)</li>
              <li><code>link</code> — real GitHub repo, doc, or demo URL (not <code>example.com</code>)</li>
              <li><code>screenshots</code> — optional images; use <code>screenshots: []</code> if you have none yet</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li><strong>To add a brand-new project</strong> (instead of editing a sample): copy the block below → place your cursor after an existing project’s closing <code>{'}'},</code> (still inside the <code>projects</code> brackets) → paste → change every sample string to your content.</li>
          <li><strong>Class assignments are fine</strong> if you describe your contribution honestly. Delete sample projects you are not using so the page only shows your work.</li>
          <li>Save, then refresh the local preview. Confirm the Projects section and (if you set a <code>slug</code>) open the project page link.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="prompt-card has-coach">
        <div class="prompt-heading"><div><span class="prompt-label">COPY · PROJECT OBJECT</span><h3>New project card (paste inside <code>projects</code> only)</h3></div><button class="copy-button" data-copy-prompt="project-object" data-copy-reset="Copy example">Copy example</button></div>
        <ol class="coach-steps">
          <li><strong>Easiest path:</strong> skip Copy — edit an existing sample project’s quoted text in place.</li>
          <li><strong>Need a brand-new card:</strong> Copy example → click after an existing project’s <code>{'}'},</code> inside <code>projects: [ ... ]</code> → paste → replace every sample string with your project.</li>
          <li><code>slug</code> is not a title — it is the URL piece (lowercase + hyphens only). <code>screenshots: []</code> means “no images yet.”</li>
        </ol>
        <pre id="project-object">{'{'}
  title: 'Inventory tracker',
  slug: 'inventory-tracker',
  summary: 'Built a spreadsheet workflow that cut weekly stock-check time for a student organization.',
  overview: 'Short story of what you built and who it helped.',
  problem: 'What was painful before this existed.',
  approach: [
    'Talked to two officers about how they counted stock.',
    'Built a simple tracker and documented the steps.',
  ],
  outcome: 'Stock checks dropped from about 45 minutes to under 15.',
  skills: ['Excel', 'Documentation'],
  link: 'https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/YOUR-REPOSITORY',
  screenshots: [],
{'}'},</pre>
        <p class="help-text">Never paste this at the top of <code>profile.js</code>. It must sit inside the <code>projects: [ ... ]</code> brackets.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-task"><span class="task-label">DO THIS · ADD A PHOTO (OPTIONAL)</span>
        <ol>
