      <details class="terminal-details">
        <summary>Terminal shows SyntaxError after editing profile.js?</summary>
        <p>That usually means a missing or extra comma in a list such as <code>coursework</code>, <code>activities</code>, <code>experience</code>, or <code>projects</code>. Check these three things:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Every object except the last one in a list ends with <code>{'}'},</code> (comma after the closing brace).</li>
          <li>The last object in a list can end with <code>{'}'}</code> or <code>{'}'},</code> — both are fine — but do not leave a lone comma with nothing after it.</li>
          <li>Strings use matching quotes: <code>'like this'</code>.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="help-text">Undo the last edit (<strong>Edit → Undo</strong>), save, and run <code>npm run dev</code> again. If it still fails, ask the facilitator before rewriting the whole file.</p>
      </details>

      <div class="step-task"><span class="task-label">CHECK BEFORE YOU CONTINUE</span>
        <ol>
          <li>Preview at desktop width and at a narrow/mobile width.</li>
          <li>Click your email, GitHub, LinkedIn, and project links — they should go to <em>your</em> pages, not leftover <code>example.com</code> placeholders.</li>
          <li>Confirm your name, sections, and photo look the way you expect.</li>
          <li>Still <strong>do not Commit</strong> in Source Control — that happens on a branch in Step 5.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

